    "skills": [
      {
        "skill": "blast-radius",
        "findings": [
          {
            "finding": "The one safety fact is that no tracked file imports jose, @vercel/oidc, the Apple library or prop-types. A git grep at the head for a static import, a dynamic import and a require of each name finds nothing outside package-lock.json. typecheck, lint, format:check, security, audit:check and build:ios-js pass on the head tree.",
            "cites": "Steps 2",
            "none": "The new packages are inert until a later change imports them."
          },
          {
            "finding": "Checked resolution with npm ls and package-lock.json. packages/server resolves its own jose 6.2.12. The root jose 5.10.0 serves only the @vercel/oidc 3.8.9 copy that @vercel/functions pulls in under @workflow/core, and that copy declares jose ^5.9.6. packages/server, @ai-sdk/gateway 4.0.100, @workflow/world-vercel and @vercel/queue share one root @vercel/oidc 3.2.0. The lockfile adds five entries: the Apple library, prop-types, object-assign, a nested react-is 16.13.1 and the packages/server jose.",
            "cites": "Steps 3",
            "none": "Each importer resolves the version it declares."
          },
          {
            "finding": "Ran the transform from packages/server/jest.config.cjs on scratch tests kept outside the repository. A static import of jwtVerify from jose fails with \"Must use import to load ES Module\", because jose 6.2.12 ships only ESM and babel-jest turns the import into a require. await import('jose') loads, and so does a type-only import, which Babel erases. A static import of @vercel/oidc 3.2.0 loads, because its dist is CommonJS.",
            "cites": "How sure are you 4",
            "none": "No module imports jose in this change. The first server module that imports it, and every test that loads that module, must use await import('jose') as jev.ts does for @ai-sdk/gateway, or change the Jest transform, which is a control change."
          },
          {
            "finding": "Ran the @react-native/jest-preset config of packages/app on a scratch test that imports the Apple library. It fails with \"Cannot use import statement outside a module\" in lib/index.js, because the preset transforms only react-native and @react-native packages under node_modules.",
            "cites": "How sure are you 4",
            "none": "No module imports the library in this change. App tests that reach the first module that imports it need a jest.mock of the library, as the existing tests do for react-native-bootsplash, or a transformIgnorePatterns change, which is a control change."
          }
        ],
